/* ZAISRV binder source. Part 7 checkpoint, lesson 07-05. See
   solutions/07-05/zaisrv.rpgle for the exported procedures'
   implementation (get / reserve / release) and their own headers for
   the full port/citation trail.

   PROVENANCE OF THIS FILE'S SHAPE: src/qsrvsrc/jucsrv.bnd (07-03's own
   binder source) now exists and is CONFIRMED on real hardware
   (part07-03-signature) - see that file's own header for the full
   EXPORT(*ALL)-vs-binder-source signature story. This file was
   originally built directly from
   work/design/refs/ileconcepts75.txt's own worked STRPGMEXP / EXPORT
   SYMBOL / ENDPGMEXP examples - specifically the "Binder Language
   Example 1" block at lines 4131-4137, and the near-identical repeat
   of the same block at lines 8810-8818 (both:
     STRPGMEXP PGMLVL(*CURRENT)
        EXPORT SYMBOL('Term')
        EXPORT SYMBOL('Rate')
        ...
     ENDPGMEXP
   with ZAISRV's own three procedure names substituted for Term/Rate/
   Amount/Payment below). If 07-03 later writes src/qsrvsrc/jucsrv.bnd,
   a future pass over this file should double check the two are
   consistent in header-comment style and simplify this provenance
   note accordingly.

   Only one STRPGMEXP block appears below, with PGMLVL(*CURRENT) -
   this is ZAISRV's first release, so there is no PGMLVL(*PRV) history
   to preserve yet (rule for exactly one PGMLVL(*CURRENT) block per
   source file: work/design/refs/ileconcepts75.txt lines 3994-3999,
   read directly this session - "Only one STRPGMEXP command can
   specify PGMLVL(*CURRENT)... All other STRPGMEXP commands within a
   source file must specify PGMLVL(*PRV)"). A future lesson (per this
   repo's 07-03 precedent: adding a procedure without breaking an
   existing signature) would, per ileconcepts75.txt lines 4287-4289
   ("1. Duplicate the STRPGMEXP, ENDPGMEXP block that contains
   PGMLVL(*CURRENT). 2. Change the duplicated PGMLVL(*CURRENT) value
   to PGMLVL(*PRV). 3. In the STRPGMEXP command that contains
   PGMLVL(*CURRENT), add to the end of the list the new symbol"):
     (1) duplicate this file's CURRENT block below as a NEW
         PGMLVL(*PRV) block, still listing all three of 'GET',
         'RESERVE', and 'RELEASE' (everything that exists at the time
         of that future change - NOT a subset), then
     (2) append the new procedure's own EXPORT SYMBOL to THIS block's
         PGMLVL(*CURRENT) list (leaving 'GET'/'RESERVE'/'RELEASE' in
         place here, unedited).
   Never edit or remove this PGMLVL(*CURRENT) block's own existing
   symbols once other programs have bound against it.

   EXPORT SYMBOL casing: 'GET', 'RESERVE', 'RELEASE' (upper case) -
   see zaisrv.rpgle's own header for the citation trail
   (work/design/refs/ilerpgref75.txt lines 31322-31324, 31334-31336,
   31381-31383: an RPG procedure with no EXTPROC/EXTPGM keyword at all
   exports under the upper-case form of its name by default). This
   resolves work/design/part07-design-v1.md section 9 item 5, which
   had flagged this casing rule as unconfirmed against
   ileconcepts75.txt's own EXPORT SYMBOL examples alone; the rule was
   instead found in ilerpgref75.txt's EXTPROC section, read directly
   this session. CONFIRMED (part07-05-checkpoint, 2026-09-27): DRIVER
   successfully bound to and called get/reserve/release via
   EXTPROC('GET')/('RESERVE')/('RELEASE') - a mismatched default
   casing would have failed to bind, so this successful build+run is
   itself the real-compile confirmation this TODO was waiting for.

   Intended member: QSRVSRC/ZAISRV (library resolved via *LIBL, per
   docs/style-guide.md - never a hardcoded library name in source).

   BUILD RECIPE (see zaisrv.rpgle's own header for the full citation
   trail - CRTBNDRPG cannot produce a *SRVPGM at all, confirmed against
   work/design/refs/cl_commands_75.txt's own CRTBNDRPG parameter
   table, so this is the two-step CRTRPGMOD-then-CRTSRVPGM path):
     CRTRPGMOD MODULE(<lib>/ZAISRV) SRCFILE(<lib>/QRPGLESRC)
       SRCMBR(ZAISRV)
     CRTSRVPGM SRVPGM(<lib>/ZAISRV) MODULE(<lib>/ZAISRV)
       EXPORT(*SRCFILE) SRCFILE(<lib>/QSRVSRC) SRCMBR(ZAISRV)
       ACTGRP(*CALLER)
   <lib> is a placeholder for the learner's own library - no real
   PUB400 library or user name appears in this file. */

STRPGMEXP PGMLVL(*CURRENT)
   EXPORT SYMBOL('GET')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('RESERVE')
   EXPORT SYMBOL('RELEASE')
ENDPGMEXP
